  "verbalization": "Procyanidin C2 is implicated in the inhibition of Phosphodiesterase 6C through multiple indirect pathways, with the CEM/C2 cell line serving as a common intermediate. The evidence suggests that Procyanidin C2 exerts its effects by targeting CEM/C2, which in turn is a target of both Pentacosanoic acid and a complex glycosylated compound. These targets ultimately interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C, indicating a potential mechanism involving the modulation of enzyme activity. The varying scores across the paths suggest that the relationship is supported by multiple layers of evidence, with the core mechanism likely involving the inhibition of Phosphodiesterase 6C through the interaction with its target in the CEM/C2 cell line. The presence of multiple targets and their shared interaction with Phosphodiesterase 6C supports a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
